      "message": "\"com.android.support.apexer\" depends on \"go\" binaries.\n\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/aosp-master/build/soong/apex/apex.go?rcl\u003d5d790c3ddad12b66ebb2e8491c042269af6f2a73\u0026l\u003d964\n\nI don\u0027t think we need \"com.android.support.apexer\" as \"zip\" apex. It looks like that it just piggy-backs on apex. Anyway, it is supported here and there like following\n \nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/aosp-master/system/apex/apexer/Android.bp?rcl\u003d80f6a25b99a44a12df5f1890922963d767d2221a\u0026l\u003d87\n\nBy the way, we can just call VisitDirectDeps() here because we decided to ignore \"testApex\" and it is the only one which depends on non-android.Module. But since we support \"go\" binaries, we\u0027d better stick to *Blueprint().",
